&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs, the company behind the open observability cloud, is founded on the principles of open source, open standards, open ecosystems, and open culture. Grafana Cloud, our fully managed observability platform, is flexible and built for scale. With Grafana Cloud&#39;s actually useful AI, organizations can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data to move at the speed of their ambitions. Today, more than 35 million users and 7,000+ customers – including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce – trust Grafana Labs to ensure reliability of their applications and systems, resolve incidents quickly, and optimize their telemetry to reduce noise and cost. We are a 100% remote company with 1,600+ team members across 40+ countries, and we’re backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fully remote position and we&#39;re considering candidates in the UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Product Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Product Manager at Grafana Labs, you&#39;ll develop a vision and strategy for your product domain. You will own your product’s roadmap, collateral, and market research, and you will collaborate with Grafana leadership on fine-tuning your product’s goals. You will be the primary advocate and expert in your area, with a strong ability to communicate needs, functionality, and details effectively both to external customers and internal stakeholders. The teams and people you will be interacting with will be 100% remote and globally distributed, so strong and proactive communication is essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Managers are the bridge that connect Engineering, Design, and UX to GTM. You are a facilitator who ensures the free flow of information across these teams and are expected to be technically proficient when representing our products to our customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Staff Product Manager for OpenTelemetry Experience, you’ll own the end-to-end journey for helping people and agents instrument workloads and successfully send useful OpenTelemetry data to Grafana Cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission is to make Grafana Cloud the easiest and most trusted destination for OpenTelemetry workloads. You’ll reduce the uncertainty, complexity, and failure points users encounter between deciding to adopt OpenTelemetry and receiving healthy, correctly attributed, and actionable telemetry in Grafana Cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teams can instrument workloads, directly or with the help of coding agents, through OpenTelemetry SDKs, automatic instrumentation technologies such as Beyla and SDK injection, or client-side OpenTelemetry Collectors. Each path presents different decisions, deployment requirements, configuration steps, and potential failure modes. You’ll define a coherent experience that helps users choose the right approach, complete setup successfully, troubleshoot problems, and understand whether their telemetry is healthy and useful. You’ll design a future in which a growing share of instrumentation work is performed by coding agents acting on behalf of developers. This means treating agents are first-class participants in the experience and ensuring that instrumentation options, configuration requirements, errors, and validation signals are structured, discoverable, and actionable by both humans and machines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your scope will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OpenTelemetry SDK onboarding and configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automatic instrumentation experiences, including OBI/Beyla and SDK injection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client-side OpenTelemetry Collector deployment and onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collector configuration, authentication, and initial connectivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guidance and machine-readable context that help people and agents choose the right instrumentation approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflows that allow coding-agents to implement, configure and verify instrumentation safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting missing, incomplete, malformed, or unhealthy telemetry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validation signals that allow both people and agents to confirm that telemetry is healthy, correctly attributed, and usable in Grafana Cloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The transition from receiving telemetry to activating the appropriate Grafana Cloud observability solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success does not stop when Grafana Cloud receives the first data point. Telemetry must arrive with the quality, context, and structure required to support meaningful observability outcomes. You’ll partner closely with teams responsible for experiences such as Application Observability, Kubernetes Monitoring, Infrastructure Observability, and Drilldown Apps to ensure OpenTelemetry workloads receive a first-class experience from initial setup through first value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a horizontal Staff-level product leadership role spanning multiple products and engineering teams. You may not directly own every SDK, collector, instrumentation technology, or downstream application involved in the journey. You will, however, be accountable for the coherence of the overall customer experience, its success measures, and the cross-product strategy required to improve it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;AI will also be part of how you work, not only what you build. You’ll be expected to use AI tools regularly to accelerate customer-research synthesis, analyze product signals, explore technical workflows, prototype experiences, develop positioning content, and test agent-led instrumentation journeys. You’ll model thoughtful, hands-on adoption of AI while applying strong judgement to its outputs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is not focused on developing OpenTelemetry as an open source project in isolation. You’ll engage with and contribute to the OpenTelemetry ecosystem where appropriate, while measuring success through customer activation and outcomes in Grafana Cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the vision, strategy, and cross-product roadmap for the journey from an uninstrumented workload to healthy, useful telemetry in Grafana Cloud solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create coherent, opinionated experiences that help users choose and implement the right approach across SDK instrumentation, automatic instrumentation, and Collector-based deployment while preserving the flexibility advanced users require&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and eliminate the leading causes of setup failure, abandonment, misconfiguration, and low-quality telemetry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish shared experience principles, priorities, and success criteria across the product and engineering teams contributing to the OpenTelemetry journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer research, product data, and market insight to prioritize investments and measure outcomes such as onboarding completion, time to useful telemetry, telemetry health, and workload expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with downstream Grafana Cloud solution teams to create a coherent transition from telemetry ingestion to meaningful product activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend beyond product delivery to how the OpenTelemetry experience is positioned and brought to market. In partnership with Product Marketing and go-to-market teams, you’ll help define the product narrative, sharpen out differentiation, and develop launches, technical content, adoption programs, and campaigns that create demand and accelerate customer activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Engineering, Design, Documentation, Developer Relations, Product Marketing, and go-to-market teams to deliver and communicate a differentiated OpenTelemetry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Grafana Labs and its customers in relevant OpenTelemetry ecosystem discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;What makes you a great fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of Product Management experience, with a strong track record in developer tools, observability, infrastructure, data platforms, or another technically complex B2B product domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading strategy and execution across multiple engineering teams or product areas without relying on direct organizational authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of OpenTelemetry, including SDK instrumentation, OTLP, Collector pipelines, telemetry context, and semantic conventions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using or building instrumentation systems, agents, telemetry collectors, configuration products, or related infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of the challenges involved in deploying and operating software across Kubernetes, virtual machines, and public cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning complex onboarding, configuration, and troubleshooting workflows into clear and approachable product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of using customer research and product data to make decisions, align stakeholders, and deliver measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence technical and nontechnical stakeholders in a remote, globally distributed organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to or building products around the OpenTelemetry or broader open source observability ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automatic instrumentation, eBPF, or runtime-based instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Firsthand experience as an SRE, platform engineer, developer, or observability practitioner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building product-led onboarding, configuration-validation, or telemetry-health experiences at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the UK, the base compensation range for this role is GBP &lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;117,949&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp; GBP 141,539&lt;/span&gt;. Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs&#39; success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and inve

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Too Good To Go, we dream of a planet with no food waste.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Did you know that more than 40% of all food produced gets thrown away? This unnecessary food waste — and the resources needed to produce and transport it — accounts for 10% of global greenhouse gas emissions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Too Good To Go is a certified B Corporation on a mission to end food waste. We connect stores with surplus food to consumers across 20 markets in Europe, North America, and APAC — with over 140 million registered users, more than 200,000 daily active stores, and 600 million meals saved from going to waste.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pricing sits at the centre of everything we do. It shapes what partners earn, what consumers pay, and how much surplus food actually gets saved. Today, pricing decisions are made in different places, for different reasons, without a single team owning the strategy end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are changing that. We are building our first dedicated Pricing team — and you will be the founding member.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will start with a concrete, high-value problem: the pricing infrastructure behind our Key Account deals. That&#39;s your launchpad — from there, you will have real scope to shape our approach to dynamic pricing, consumer-facing service fees, and pricing strategy across Too Good To Go more broadly. This is a role built for someone who wants to define a domain, not just execute a brief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The goal behind everything we do is twofold: save as much surplus food as possible, and grow the pie between TGTG, our Partners, and our Consumers — never trading one off against the other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is a further dimension to this. We are expanding beyond food into new non-food, non-perishable categories — and that growth brings pricing complexity and opportunity we have not had to solve before. Getting ahead of that, rather than reacting to it, is part of this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Product Manager for Pricing, you will build the foundation for how Too Good To Go prices its marketplace — starting with Key Account deals, then extending across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the near term, you will design and ship the infrastructure that lets us set, manage, and evolve pricing for Key Account partnerships with the flexibility our commercial teams need. From there, you will develop a smarter, more dynamic pricing algorithm that responds to supply, demand, and partner economics — replacing static rules with something genuinely intelligent. Alongside this, you will investigate our consumer-facing service fees: how they&#39;re structured, how they&#39;re perceived, and where there is room to optimise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Underneath all of it are two questions you will own: how do we price in a way that saves as much surplus food as possible, and how do we grow the pie for everyone — Too Good To Go, our Partners, and our Consumers — rather than shifting value from one side to another? Answering both well means understanding marketplace pricing broadly: the best practices and patterns other two- and three-sided marketplaces use, and what applies to ours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pricing decisions rarely stay inside one product&#39;s boundaries, so you will work across product teams and the wider organisation — Commercial, Data Science, Engineering, Finance, and Key Accounts — to make sure pricing is right everywhere it shows up, not just within your own roadmap. You will become the go-to person for anything pricing-related at Too Good To Go, including presenting your strategy and results to the Global Management Team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also help lay the pricing groundwork for our move into non-food, non-perishable categories — different cost structures, margins, and purchase patterns than the food pricing we know today, and a chance to shape pricing thinking for a new part of the business from the start.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the founding Pricing PM, operating as an individual contributor, with a small dedicated engineering team of around 3-4 developers to start. We will grow the team&#39;s scope and headcount as we prove impact, not before. You will report directly to our VP of Product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a new team with a clear starting point, not a fixed script. You will know where to begin — Key Account deals — but how the team&#39;s remit, roadmap, and impact grow from there is largely yours to shape. If you want a role where everything is already solved and you are just executing, this isn&#39;t it. If you want to help define what great pricing looks like across Too Good To Go, it is.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is suited to someone who does not need daily direction — who can set the agenda within that mandate, manage up effectively, and make strong pricing calls with incomplete information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the pricing infrastructure for Key Account deals, giving commercial teams the tools and flexibility to structure partnerships well while keeping pricing logic sound and scalable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop a smart pricing algorithm — moving from static, rules-based pricing toward a dynamic model informed by supply, demand, and partner-specific economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate consumer-facing service fees: how they&#39;re set, how they perform, and how they should evolve to balance consumer value with business sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a holistic view of pricing across TGTG, Partners, and Consumers — optimising for meals saved and for growing the pie for all three, rather than trading one off against another.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and apply best practices and patterns from marketplace pricing more broadly, adapting proven approaches to our specific dynamics rather than reinventing from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap and OKRs for the Pricing team within its agreed mandate, sequencing the work so that early wins on Key Accounts build toward the algorithm and fee strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across product teams and the wider organisation — Commercial, Data Science, Engineering, Finance, and Key Accounts — to make sure pricing decisions are right wherever they show up, not just within your own roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the go-to person for anything pricing-related at Too Good To Go, including presenting strategy, models, and results to the Global Management Team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate the pricing complexity and opportunity of TGTG&#39;s expansion into non-food, non-perishable categories, and start laying the groundwork for pricing them well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data rigorously — pricing experiments, elasticity analysis, partner and consumer feedback — to test hypotheses before scaling them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-year experience in Product Management with direct, hands-on ownership of pricing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with pricing in a marketplace or platform business is a genuine differentiator. If you&#39;ve worked on take rates, dynamic pricing, two-sided pricing trade-offs, or fee structures in a marketplace, you will hit the ground running.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building pricing algorithms, models, or infrastructure — not just adjusting numbers in a spreadsheet, but shipping systems that price things well and can evolve over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with quantitative teams (data science, analytics, finance) to translate pricing theory into production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable — and genuinely thrive — working independently, with a high degree of autonomy, especially in the early stages of building a new team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring a rigorous, quantitative mind. You reason from first principles about supply, demand, and incentives, and you back your recommendations with data and clear models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can hold multiple stakeholders&#39; interests in view at once — TGTG&#39;s, our Partners&#39;, and our Consumers&#39; — and make the case for a solution that works for all three.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build genuine working relationships across product and the wider business, not just within your own team, so that pricing is done right wherever it touches the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an excellent communicator, comfortable presenting to senior and executive audiences — including the Global Management Team — with clarity and confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You move fast. You do not wait for perfect information. You are decisive, transparent about your reasoning, and quick to adjust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a growth mindset. You are always looking for the next level — in the pricing model, in the strategy, and in yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are genuinely fun to work with. You bring your authentic self, you care about the mission, and you know how to succeed as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We win together: food waste is a big beast to fight. We can do it if we win together as Waste Warriors with no ego. We believe in #oneteam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We raise the bar: we always push for more. We work smart, smash barriers, and elevate one another.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We keep it simple: our ambitions are bold but our solutions are simple.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We build a legacy: we are proud of the change we are driving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We care: we always look out for each other. Caring is also about the way we do business. We do the right thing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Have to Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A rare opportunity to work in a social impact company (and certified B Corporation!) where you get to wake up every day knowing you are achieving positive change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to build something genuinely new — a first-of-its-kind Pricing team, with a clear mandate and real influence over how the business grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership over decisions that touch every side of our marketplace, from Key Account partnerships to millions of consumers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The experience of being part of an international company with 1,200+ enthusiastic and highly talented teammates across 22 countries — always ready to share knowledge and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong personal and professional development in an intense and high-growth scale-up environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An open company culture where you have the independence and room to unleash your creativity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong team culture where successes are celebrated together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to Apply&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We take recruitment very seriously, so please carefully read everything we have written abov

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;Founded in 2020, unybrands is the next-generation brand accelerator platform built to acquire, integrate, and scale digital-first consumer brands. Headquartered in Miami, with offices in New York, London, Berlin, and Shenzhen, our 240+ team brings deep expertise across e-commerce, brand management, consumer retail, operational scaling, and M&amp;amp;A.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;Since inception, we have acquired 30+ brands across Pet Care, Personal Care, Home Care, Supplements, Baby &amp;amp; Juvenile, Garden &amp;amp; Outdoor, Sports &amp;amp; Fitness, and Home &amp;amp; Lifestyle — completing 20+ acquisitions and delivering 16 consecutive quarters of like-for-like organic growth post-integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;Our competitive advantage lies in a fully integrated operating system purpose-built to transform digital brands into omni-channel category leaders. Powered by a proprietary technology stack built on NetSuite ERP with 200+ data integrations, our platform enables brands to thrive across marketplaces, direct-to-consumer channels, and brick-and-mortar retail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]&quot;&gt;We focus on acquiring digital-first brands within carefully selected verticals, then applying tailored value creation playbooks that drive growth through innovation, expansion, and automation. We believe the next generation of consumer brands will be built differently — and we&#39;re building the AI-enabled retail tech platform to help them consolidate and win.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Counsel (M&amp;amp;A) will be responsible for providing general advice across all functions, with a focus on executing on unybrands’ acquisitions. The primary responsibilities will be enhancing leading on legal workstreams of our acquisition process from letter of intent, through to diligence, transaction document preparation, negotiation and execution. Moreover, the role will involve general in-house matters (commercial contracts, employment matters, intellectual property, data privacy, etc). The candidate would also be expected to be able to assist the General Counsel in equity and debt matters (including in respect of the negotiation of any future equity or debt finance rounds for unybrands).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have the opportunity to work cross functionally across the company and contribute to important strategic initiatives as well as operational matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*this job might require you to travel to Hemel Hempstead office occasionally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities include - but not limited to:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the negotiating and drafting of acquisition contracts for ecommerce brands being folded into the unybrands portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the General Counsel on corporate finance matters (equity and debt).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the negotiating and drafting of contracts customary to a fast-growing ecommerce startup with a primary focus on commercial contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, revise and negotiate a range of complex corporate and commercial agreements, including warehousing, marketing, IT, licensing, services, consulting, supply, confidentiality, collaboration, research, and data-related agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide legal support across the organization, including quickly and effectively identifying complex legal and compliance issues and providing advice in a manner that integrates legal risk management with the company’s business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with outside counsel on intellectual property and data privacy matters and ensure execution of action plans and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance existing policies, processes, and templates, as well as training employees with respect thereto and implementing the processes and templates on our technology platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate both within the legal team and with business clients to develop or enhance a variety of contract templates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage outside counsel as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain strong business relationships across the company and contribute to cross-functional or departmental projects and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the legal and compliance teams with a variety of legal matters, including general corporate, compliance, regulatory and other legal matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support efforts to effectively manage the delivery of legal services including budgeting, recruiting, performance management, process improvements, operations, training and team building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A successful team member will have:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified solicitor (England &amp;amp; Wales or any other common law jurisdiction) and 3+ years of experience as a legal counsel with experience managing M&amp;amp;A processes, drafting and negotiating M&amp;amp;A documents, drafting a variety of commercial contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A combination of law firm and in-house experience would be ideal. Excellent interpersonal and client relations skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with employment law is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working for, or in, a high growth (start-up / venture capital) environment would be preferred, albeit not essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced environment leveraging internal and external resources to meet simultaneous deadlines/demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with implementing a contract management system; creating and managing contract templates; training business partners on contract policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent research, writing, counseling and communication skills and a positive client service orientation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently, as a team member, and across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountability, sound judgment, and the ability to take ownership of an issue and provide concise and timely advice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills would be a value-add.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;role&quot;&gt;
&lt;section id=&quot;role&quot;&gt;
